From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Gyuyoung Kim <qkim@google.com>
Date: Tue, 22 Sep 2026 04:03:37 +0000
Subject: [M150-LTS] bluetooth: Fix reentrancy UAF during ShowPermissionPrompt

When a renderer requests Bluetooth scanning via
navigator.bluetooth.requestLEScan(), the browser service synchronously
calls the embedder delegate's ShowBluetoothScanningPrompt() method.
Displaying the desktop scanning prompt drops fullscreen, which can spin
a nested message loop while exiting fullscreen mode across related tabs.

During this nested message loop, pending IPCs (such as an iframe
removal FrameDetach IPC) can be processed synchronously, destroying the
requesting subframe's RenderFrameHostImpl and its associated service
objects, including BluetoothDeviceScanningPromptController. When
ShowBluetoothScanningPrompt() returns, assigning the prompt into
prompt_ causes a heap-use-after-free write on the deleted controller.

This CL captures a base::WeakPtr to the controller before calling
ShowBluetoothScanningPrompt() and verifies liveness before accessing
member fields.

TAG=agy
CONV=3182e656-edea-4b6d-aa62-f521ce8320bc

Fixed: 554558320
